# charter.registry — GATE-CHARTER's grandfather table and dotfile allowlist (AUDIT 2026-10-01,
# docs/dev/evidence/rmbp-0929/AUDIT-HANDLERS-UNAFS.md). A kernel file in the APP-DOMAIN scope
# (video/, fs/, install/, selfhost/, help.rs, termcolor.rs, shellux.rs, clipboard.rs, shell.rs,
# drivers/hda_play.rs) must carry a `CHARTER:` header line or a row here. Rows here are the files
# that existed BEFORE the gate; a NEW file never gets a row — it declares in its own header.
#
# file | <CODEX handler or Kernel> | <seam> | <ref>
#   seam: wm (window manager / compositor / glass — the kernel's own), driver, fs-core (the VFS and
#   the volume code), shared-core (a no_std lib both rings link), fulfiller (the kernel fulfils the
#   owner's bus verbs), kernel-by-ruling (R-id), owed (the audit row that says it must move)
video/activity.rs | pulse | owed | B289
video/appmenu.rs | Kernel | wm | menus (crystal.rs: the bandy menu protocol is a later arc)
video/beam.rs | Kernel | wm | compositor
video/brightkeys.rs | Principia | owed | B287 (brightness is a preference)
video/ceramic.rs | Kernel | wm | theme/paint
video/clipboard.rs | Kernel | wm | one text buffer; no handler owns it
video/crystal.rs | Kernel | wm | menus
video/cursor.rs | Kernel | wm | pointer
video/desktop_firmware.rs | Kernel | wm | aarch64 desktop ignition
video/desktop_uefi.rs | Kernel | wm | x86 desktop ignition
video/dimidle.rs | Principia | owed | B287 (idle blank is a preference)
video/dock.rs | Kernel | wm | the dock strip; its pins file is B287
video/facet.rs | Facet | owed | B289 (documented in its header: the vessel is std/WGPU)
video/fbcon.rs | Kernel | wm | framebuffer console
video/fileview.rs | Tabula | owed | B289
video/font.rs | Kernel | wm | glyphs
video/framebuffer.rs | Kernel | wm | surface
video/instgui.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296 (the installer ensemble)
video/keymap.rs | Kernel | driver | HID decode
video/knurl.rs | Kernel | wm | controls
video/login.rs | Holocron | kernel-by-ruling | R51/R62/R64 — the login screen is the kernel's until Holocron exists
video/menubar.rs | Kernel | wm | menubar
video/mod.rs | Kernel | wm | module root
video/paper.rs | Kernel | wm | wallpaper paint; the wallpaper choice is B287
video/png.rs | Kernel | shared-core | PNG/deflate codec (lux is the host twin; one codec owed)
video/powerui.rs | Kernel | wm | power menu; battery thresholds are a Principia preference (B287)
video/prtscr.rs | Kernel | wm | screenshot capture
video/pulsewin.rs | pulse | owed | B289
video/quarry.rs | Matrix | kernel-by-ruling | R50 "quarry is our finder" (B288)
video/quarry/live.rs | Matrix | kernel-by-ruling | R50 (B288); opener routing is B293
video/quarry/ops.rs | Matrix | kernel-by-ruling | R50 (B288)
video/screen.rs | Kernel | wm | glass
video/settings.rs | Principia | owed | B287
video/shortcuts.rs | Kernel | wm | chord table and overlay
video/shotsel.rs | Kernel | wm | screenshot region
video/status.rs | Kernel | wm | status line
video/strip.rs | Kernel | wm | dock strip
video/termsel.rs | Midden | shared-core | selection over the shell line (midden_core is the verb side)
video/textedit.rs | Tabula | owed | B289
video/theme.rs | Kernel | wm | theme tables
video/vperf.rs | Kernel | wm | compositor perf
video/wallpaper.rs | Principia | owed | B287
video/wcf.rs | Kernel | wm | compositor
video/wcg.rs | Kernel | wm | compositor
video/wcpar.rs | Kernel | wm | compositor
video/winlist.rs | Kernel | wm | window menu
video/winmenu.rs | Kernel | wm | window menu
video/winsnap.rs | Kernel | wm | snapping
video/witness.rs | Kernel | wm | witness lines
video/wm.rs | Kernel | wm | the window manager
fs/bootdisk.rs | Kernel | fs-core | root binding
fs/fat.rs | Kernel | fs-core | FAT volume
fs/fatperf.rs | Kernel | fs-core | FAT bench
fs/holocron.rs | Holocron | owed | B296 (the kernel-side record store; the handler is design-only)
fs/mod.rs | Kernel | fs-core | module root
fs/sdhc4c.rs | Kernel | driver | card seam
fs/trash.rs | Matrix | owed | B288
fs/unafs.rs | Kernel | fs-core | the UnaFS mount (shared-core: unaos/libs/fs/unafs)
fs/users.rs | Holocron | owed | B296
fs/vfs.rs | Kernel | fs-core | the mount table
install/clone.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296
install/fat32.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296
install/gpt.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296
install/mod.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296
install/partition.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296
install/pi.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296
install/selfguard.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296
install/selfinstall.rs | Amber Bytes | owed | B296
selfhost/extract.rs | Geode | owed | B296
selfhost/inflate.rs | Geode | owed | B296 (one deflate with video/png.rs owed)
selfhost/mod.rs | Geode | owed | B296
selfhost/tar.rs | Geode | owed | B296
help.rs | Midden | shared-core | midden_core verb tables
termcolor.rs | Midden | shared-core | SGR on the console
shellux.rs | Midden | shared-core | line editing
shell.rs | Midden | shared-core | the verb dispatch (GATE-VERBS keeps it one set with HOST_VERBS)
drivers/hda_play.rs | Stria | owed | B289
# dotfile | <name as the literal spells it> | <ref> — every `<home>/.name` literal the kernel writes
dotfile | .settings | B287 (moves to Principia's store)
dotfile | .dock | B287
dotfile | .holocron | B448 (HOLOCRONROOT: the one secrets root, named in holocron_core::root)
dotfile | .Trash | B288
dotfile | .Trash/.index | B288 → TRASHTIME (B308): FAT fallback only; on UnaFS trash state is attributes on the object
dotfile | .index | B288 → TRASHTIME (B308): FAT fallback only
dotfile | .config/unaos/preferences.toml | B300 (Principia's path — the ONE preference store, PREFS)
dotfile | .new | swap-temp suffix of the atomic write pattern (USERS.NEW shape; prefs.rs), not a dotfile
